# Copy this file to .env and fill in a real RPC URL per chain.
# Never commit .env — it is gitignored.
#
# A PRODUCTION-CLASS provider (Alchemy / Infura / QuickNode class) is required
# for the AccessControl event-reconstruction path: it needs eth_getLogs over
# wide block ranges, which public endpoints (e.g. blastapi) cap at ~10 blocks.
# Ripcord probes the provider's real getLogs range at startup and chunks to it
# (see src/chain/rpcPreflight.ts); on a capped public endpoint the role-history
# scan degrades to an explicitly-labelled partial reconstruction, never a
# silent failure. The provider name (host only, never the key) is printed at
# the start of every scan.
#
# Determinism is provider-independent: every read is pinned to a block and
# cached by (chainId, block, method, params) — NOT by provider — so a warm
# cache built with one provider is a valid, identical hit for another.

RPC_URL_1=https://your-mainnet-rpc-provider.example/v2/YOUR_KEY
